Why This Is Asked

Tests practical multi-tenant isolation, per-tenant offset management, and resilience in KCNA with simple backpressure and testing.

Key Concepts

- Per-tenant isolation and routing
- Token-bucket rate limiting per tenant
- Durable per-tenant offsets and recovery
- Idempotent processing with robust retries
- Lightweight test harness simulating downstream lag

Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: per-tenant rate limiter and offset store
class TenantState {
  constructor(tenant, rate) {
    this.tenant = tenant;
    this.offsets = new Map(); // topic -> offset
    this.limiter = new TokenBucket(rate); // per-tenant rate
  }
  canConsume() { return this.limiter.tryConsume(this.tenant); }
  commitOffset(topic, offset) { this.offsets.set(topic, offset); }
}
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate) {
    this.rate = rate; this.tokens = rate; this.last = Date.now();
  }
  tryConsume() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.rate, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= 1) { this.tokens -= 1; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

